Hi guys,

Just posting to let you know that I found this old gauntlet of YANI someone 
carelessly dropped, and decided to wear it, it turned out to be cursed, but 
+3.  Now it's forcing me to implement the idea.
A telnet client that accepts standard nethack input from a server, does it's 
whizbang behind the scenes so that the user sees tiled output.  I envision 
it as watching the top line, and routing the messages to a scrollable 
message window with a short (say 100 lines) history, minus the '--more--' 
prompts.  It'll automagically send a space in response to '--more--' so that 
the effect (hopefully) will be the way the game works in tiled mode, with 
messages flying by that you scrollback to read at your leisure.

Next, it'll take the characters sent to the main screen area, below line 1, 
above line 23, and render them into tiles, using a hidden ';' command to 
clarify characters with multiple associations.

Line 23 and Line 24 will be parsed and sent to equivalent graphical status 
lines, with color coding where available.  The only part that's going to be 
broken is the status messages.  When you play tiled nethack from nethackw, 
it has access to the status messages 'Satiated','Confused','Stunned' and 
whatnot.  In text mode, if more than two of these pop up, it flies into 
nowhere, and nethack trims the string so that it doesn't unintentionally 
scroll the screen.  Since I'd just be parsing, tiled telnet would run into 
that limitation, too.
I *could* smooth it out a little by watching for specific messages, combined 
with parsing.  'Wow!  Everything looks so cosmic!' -> Hallucinating, 
'Everything looks so boring now.'->clear hallucinating.
Of course 'you feel better' can be ambiguous.  I think it'll be playable, 
tho.

Inventory lists will get their own windows, but the behavior won't be the 
same as true tiled, because non tiled uses pages, whereas tiled puts the 
whole inventory into a window, and leaves it up to the windowing interface. 
with tiled telnet, there'll be a button to select the next and/or previous 
page (did everyone already know that you could go back a page in an 
inventory listing?!  I just found that out accidentally a couple games ago!)

Ditto with the 'you see here' lists.  single items and small lists get 
routed to the message window, bigger lists, a 'you see here' window.

Same also with the spell list, and the enhance list.  Options will be 
somewhat problematic.  May just switch it to text mode when the user hits 
shift-O.  Alt-O will send '#offer', Alt-P '#pray', 'Are you sure' prompts 
will be captured and dialogged.  Pay whom? and other commands that require a 
location will allow the user to move the cursor via mouse or keyboard. 
Clicking on a known location in the map will
map to '_' followed by the location, to invoke the travel command.

The whole thing is complicated, but doable, so unless I can find a scroll of 
remove curse, or destroy armor, or a magic marker with enough charges, I 
guess I'm stuck with these gauntlets of YANI.

Wish me luck!  Right now I've got the framework window set up, and 
displaying a black window
with white text.  I'm off to refresh my memory of ANSI screen codes, I'm 
gonna need em!

